-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",398,{
[12705]="70020C8E\n1\tTalk to Grufudh at Gavar Cadlus\tGrufudh is at Gavar Cadlus, north-east of Echad Saeradan. Saeradan instructed you to speak with Grufudh about the banner of the White Hand that you found near Gwyllion's Gate.\n2\tTalk to Gwyllion at her hut\tGwyllion's Gate, the entrance to the path which leads to Gwyllion's hut, lies to the south of Gavar Cadlus. Grufudh told you to speak with Gwyllion, the Old Woman of the Mountain, if you wished to know the source of the White Hand banner.\n3\tTalk to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan\tSaeradan is at Echad Saeradan, west of Gwyllion's Gate. You should return to Saeradan with news of your discovery of the Uruk-hai Filskûm at Gwyllion's hut.\n",
[12706]="7006566C\n1\tInvestigate the boar-wallow near Halach\tIrodon has asked you to investigate a boar wallow to the north-east of Halach.\n2\tTalk to Asórkho near the boar wallow\tYou have found a Haradrim man near the boar wallow. You should talk to him.\n",
[12707]="7001AD28\n1\tTalk to Ianudirel to assist in her escape\tIanudirel may be found on the far side of the river from Krul Lugu. Iavassúl has asked you to find Ianudirel, his sister, and help her to return safely, if she still lives.\n2\tTalk to Iavassúl at Iavassúl's Watch\tIavassúl is at Iavassúl's Watch in Taur Morvith. You should report to Iavassúl regarding his sister's rescue.\n",
[12708]="70057E62\n1\tLearn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred\tErebor can be found in Dale-lands. You should learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred.\n2\tTalk to Léothred in Erebor\tLéothred can be found in Erebor. You should talk to Léothred in Erebor.\n3\tLearn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred\tErebor can be found in Dale-lands. You should learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred.\n4\tTalk to Léothred in Erebor\tLéothred can be found in Erebor. You should talk to Léothred in Erebor.\n",
[12709]="7002FD76\n1\tCollect food-stores around Garsfeld (total: 10)\tFood-stores can be found scattered about Garsfeld and inside the homes of the town. Gísling wants you to gather food-stores in preparation to evacuate Garsfeld. He has asked that you try to avoid the attention of the crofters so as not to incite panic.\n2\tTalk to Gísling at the Mead Hall of Garsfeld\tGísling awaits your return in the Mead Hall of Garsfeld. You should bring the rations you collected to Gísling.\n",
[12710]="7004A908\n1\tCollect spider remains (total: 5)\tUngol Weavers can be found in one of the caverns of Torech Ungol, beneath Nelegroth. You should defeat Ungol Weavers and collect their remains.\n2\tPlace the remains on the Offering Stone\030Defeat the Nelegroth Brood-mother\tThe Offering Stone can be found in one of the caverns of Torech Ungol, beneath Nelegroth. You should place the spider remains on the Offering Stone and then defeat the Nelegroth Brood-mother.\n",
[12711]="70058A46\n1\tDestroy the worm nests found in Nathból\tThe nesting grounds of Nathból can be found in Elderslade. You should destroy the worm nests found in Nathból.\n2\tDestroy the worm nests found in Nathból (total: 10)\tThe nesting grounds of Nathból can be found in Elderslade. You should destroy the worm nests found in Nathból.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed many worm nests in Nathból.\n",
[12712]="70054797\n1\tSpeak to the new recruit\tA new recruit has come to Díngarth. You should speak with the recruit.\n2\tSpeak to the new recruit\tA new recruit has come to Díngarth. You should speak with the recruit.\n3\tAssist Gelvira at Díngarth\030Assist Radigond at Díngarth\030Assist Hildvar at Díngarth\030Use the whistle to summon the new recruit if you become separated\tTake the new recruit with you as you assist those in Díngarth.\n4\tAssist Durin IV at Echad-in-Edhil with: Heraldry of Durin IV\030Assist Durin IV at Echad-in-Edhil with: Sauron's Presence Upon Parth Daenath\030Defeat foes in Parth Daenath (total: 10)\030Use the whistle to summon the new recruit if you become separated\tTake the new recruit with you as you assist those in Echad-in-Edhil.\n5\tAssist Huneric at Adambel with: Heraldry of The Thíuda\030Assist Huneric at Adambel with: Turning Defectors\030Defeat foes in Arandor (total: 10)\030Use the whistle to summon the new recruit if you become separated\tTake the new recruit with you as you assist those in Adambel.\n6\tDefeat foes in Emyn Duir (total: 15)\030Use the whistle to summon the new recruit if you become separated\tDefeat enemies in Emyn Duir.\n7\tSpeak to the new recruit\030Use the whistle to summon the new recruit if you become separated\tSpeak to the new recruit.\n",
[12713]="70045FE6\n1\tCollect supplies (total: 10)\tYou should find and collect any loose supplies that you may come across in the First Circle of Minas Tirith.\n2\tDeliver supplies to the cart\tThe supply cart can be found near the City Stables in the First Circle of Minas Tirith. You should load the cart with the supplies that you have found.\n3\tSpeak with Húrin\tHúrin can be found outside the front gates of Minas Tirith. You should report back to Húrin.\n",
[12714]="70034D0A\n1\tFind Gárnoth's Farm\tGárnoth's Farm is south of Forlaw. When taking the road south out of Forlaw, the first road to the right goes to Gárnoth's Farm.\n2\tSearch Gárnoth's Farm for signs of Núrzum\tSomewhere on Gárnoth's Farm there could be signs of Núrzum having been there. Gárnoth's Farm is south of Forlaw. When taking the road south out of Forlaw, the first road to the right goes to Gárnoth's Farm.\n3\tFollow Núrzum's trail\tNúrzum recently made a trail through Gárnoth's Farm. The path of footprints starts near the road toward Gárnoth's Farm.\n4\tDefeat Núrzum's Lieutenant\tThe Lieutenant of Núrzum is leading the forces occupying Gárnoth's Farm, and was found at the end of the trail made by Núrzum.\n5\tReturn to Cyneberg in Lornsettle\tCyneberg is keeping Gárwig company in Lornsettle, the mead hall of Forlaw.\n",
[12715]="7005D3FB\n1\tTalk to Javatar\tBy completing this quest, you will be marked as completing The Nine\n",
[12716]="7005A64E\n1\tMaergrind, the Noble Gate of Máttugard, can be found in Gundabad. You should familiarize yourself with the foothold at Maergrind.\t\n2\tTalk to Prince Ingór at Maergrind\tPrince Ingór can be found at Maergrind in Máttugard. You should talk to Prince Ingór.\n",
[12717]="70035213\n1\tSpeak with Humbald, grandson of Reeve Gárwig\030Speak with Grimgar, grandson of Reeve Gárwig\030Speak with Gársig, son of Reeve Gárwig\tThe kin of the Reeve of Wildermore can be found in Scylfig. You should see if the Reeve's son or grandsons need any assistance.\n2\tSpeak with Cyneberg\tCyneberg can be found sharpening her sword in Scylfig. You should speak with Cyneberg.\n",
[12718]="70060D87\n1\tCollect the Yonder-watch supplies from the secret store-hole\tYonder-watch supplies can be found at the secret store-hole in the woods between Gamwich and Long Cleeve. You should carry Yonder-watch supplies to Salga Greengrass in Nobottle. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Salga Greengrass in Nobottle\tSalga Greengrass can be found in Nobottle. You should talk to Salga Greengrass in Nobottle.\n3\tConfront Harry Goatleaf\tHarry Goatleaf can be found near Nobottle in the Yondershire. You should confront Harry Goatleaf.\n4\tTalk to Fredegar in Nobottle\tFredegar Bolger can be found in the village of Nobottle. You should talk to Fredegar Bolger in Nobottle.\n",
[12719]="700156B0\n1\tDefeat gredbyg in the Palace of Náin (total: 12)\tA swarm of gredbyg can likely be found in a hive in the Palance of Náin, north of Lamab-dûm in the Great Delving. Thórhall wants you to kill off as many gredbyg as you can.\n2\tReturn to Thórhall at Lamab-dûm\tThórhall is at his camp in Lamab-dûm in the Great Delving. You should return to Thórhall and tell him that the grodbog presence is somewhat lessened in the hive to the north.\n",
[12720]="700442A3\n1\tPlant banners of Gondor (total: 3)\tBanner posts can be found along the Rammas. You should place banners of Gondor on top of the Rammas.\n",
[12721]="700442A2\n1\tDefeat Hurasâna\030Defeat Kaskhâr\tSûhalar captains can be found along the Rammas. You should defeat Sûhalar captains on top of the Rammas.\n",
[12722]="700442A8\n1\tRemove hooks from the Rammas (total: 10)\tSûhalar hooks can be found along the Rammas. You should remove hooks from the top of the Rammas.\n",
[12723]="700442A5\n1\tDestroy Sûhalar supplies (total: 12)\tSûhalar supplies can be found along the Rammas. You should destroy Sûhalar supplies on top of the Rammas.\n",
[12724]="700442A4\n1\tDefeat Sûhalar warriors (total: 16)\tSûhalar warriors can be found along the Rammas. You should defeat Sûhalar warriors on top of the Rammas.\n",
[12725]="700001B1\n1\tTalk to Eiláf\tMyrkworth lies in Imlad Balchorth atop a high hill, north of Gabilshathûr. Hwati has asked you to travel to Myrkworth and speak with his cousin, Eiláf.\n",
[12726]="70041178\n1\tTalk to Melril in northern Tarlang's Crown\tMelril can be found along the path leading through Tarlang's Crown, to the south-west of Sardol in Blackroot Vale. Harnion has asked you to seek Melril in northern Tarlang's Crown and aid the people of Blackroot Vale.\n",
[12727]="700514B7\n1\tTalk to the shade of the Oath-breaker captain\tThe shade of the Oath-breaker captain can be found north-east of Mincham's camp, in some scattered ruins by the walls of Fornost. Mincham has asked you to find the shade of the Oath-breaker captain and recall him and his followers to their ancient duty.\n2\tTalk to Mincham\tMincham awaits you at his camp. The Oath-breaker captain told you that he and his followers had sworn a new allegiance to someone named Amarthiel. Mincham may know what this means.\n",
[12728]="7002C651\n1\tConfront and defeat Melethron\tMelethron is at the northern Oathbreaker camp among his fallen men. Idmar asked you to speak with the shade of Melethron.\n2\tConfront and defeat Thinnas\tThinnas is at the eastern camp of Oathbreakers near the Rushgore. Idmar has asked you to speak with the shade of Thinnas.\n3\tConfront and defeat Camlann\tCamlann is at the western camp of Oathbreakers near the border to Eorlsmead. Idmar asked you to speak with the shade of Camlann.\n4\tTalk to Idmar\tIdmar is at his camp along the road in central Parth Celebrant. You should return to Idmar with news of your dealings with the maddened shades.\n",
[12729]="700001BB\n1\tDefeat worms (total: 10)\030Defeat Ulkrank\tUlkrank, the ancient Gorthorog, can be found somewhere in the depths of the cave. Bethad has asked you to explore the cave, until you are able to find and slay Ulkrank himself.\n2\tTalk to Fonn\tFonn is back at Tyrn Lhuig. Having defeated Ulkrank, Bethad asked you to tell his friend Fonn of your deeds.\n",
[12730]="70000158\n1\tTalk to Edilina Proudfoot\tEdilina Proudfoot's hole is east of the Great Smials. Adelard sent you to ask his niece, Edilina Proudfoot, to prepare a plate of spiced boar ribs to appease the ghost of the Old Took, but warned you not to tell her the reason. He does not want to start a panic.\n2\tBring the boar-ribs to Edilina Proudfoot\030Collect boar-ribs (total: 3)\tBoars can be found in the hills east of Tuckborough. Edilina Proudfoot's home is just east of Tuckborough. Edilina Proudfoot said she could make the spiced boar-ribs that Adelard wants to appease the ghost of the Old Took, but lacks the actual ribs. She asked you to bring her some ribs from the boars in the hills beyond Tuckborough.\n3\tBring the spiced boar-ribs to Adelard Took\tAdelard Took is waiting at the Great Smials in Tuckborough. After gathering the ribs Edilina Proudfoot needed, she cooked up a plate of spiced boar-ribs for you to give to Adelard Took. You should bring them to Adelard, so he can use them to try and appease the Old Took's ghost.\n",
[12731]="70066943\n1\tCollect pebbles (total: 8)\030Collect a piece of driftwood\tYou should help Merúd collect pebbles and a piece of driftwood. These can be found along Melgobas' shore.\n2\tTalk to Merúd\tYou have collected enough pebbles and driftwood. You should return to Merúd at Melgobas' shore.\n",
[12732]="70020C8F\n1\tTalk to Saeradan to journey to Gwyllion's hut\t\n2\tTalk to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan\tSaeradan is at Echad Saeradan in the Windfells of Enedwaith. You should return to Saeradan with news of your victory against Gwyllion.\n",
[12733]="7004A81B\n1\tDefeat Thorakó, the Hewer\030Defeat Shatúrro, the Spear\tIngold has asked you to defeat the leaders of Fushaum Tûm.\n",
[12734]="70037E94\n1\tFind the trail of the rumoured boar\tThe boar was last rumoured to be in the wooded hills to the east of Aldburg. Arcil has asked that you follow the tales of a great boar, not unlike the Boar of Everholt, to see if it truly exists.\n2\tContinue to follow the trail of the great boar\tThe trail continues east into the woods. You should follow the trail of the great boar.\n3\tFollow the trail of the great boar deeper into the woods\tThe trail continues south into the woods. You should follow the trail of the great boar.\n4\tSearch for evidence of the great boar\tYou saw the silhouette of what appears to be an enormous boar nearby and should approach with caution.\n5\tTalk to Arcil\tArcil is in the Mead Hall of Aldburg, west of the woods. You should return to Arcil and let him know what you found in the woods.\n",
[12735]="7005990C\n1\tTalk to Elrond\tElrond can be found in his library in the Last Homely House. You should talk to Elrond.\n2\tFind Lothrandir in Forochel\tLothrandir can be found outside the village of Sûri-kylä in Forochel. You should find Lothrandir and explain Elrond's request.\n3\tComplete 'Instance: Dúnedain Past and Present'\tLothrandir is prepared to travel to the shipwreck of the Thoroval to meet Arvedui. Speak with Lothrandir at Sûri-kylä to enter 'Instance: Dúnedain Past and Present'.\n4\tTalk to Lothrandir\tLothrandir is with the shade of Arvedui at the shipwreck of the Thoroval. You should talk to Lothrandir.\n",
[12736]="7000D3C5\n1\tDefeat Ongbúrz Orcs in Fasach-falroid (total: 6)\030Defeat Angmarim in Fasach-falroid (total: 4)\tOrcs of the Ongbúrz tribe and their Iron Crown allies can be found in and around the city of Dûn Covád, far to the north of Aughaire, in the western hills. Guirmán has asked you to combat the foes of the Trév Gállorg that can be found in Fasach-falroid.\n2\tTalk to Guirmán\tGuirmán is at the Búth Luikh of Aughaire, far to the south of Dûn Covád. You have defeated many Ongbúrz Orcs and their Iron Crown allies and should return now to Guirmán with word of your victories.\n",
})
